title: Fernhill — RESTART reboots the story (ADR-248 acceptance)
story: fernhill
continues: arrival
description: The original Chord-path restart repro (restart used to throw
  "assignRoom: room 'r01' not found" under the hood and render as "I don't
  understand that."). Under ADR-248 the client/harness reboots with a fully
  fresh ChordStory rebuilt from source, so restart acks and the opening state
  comes back clean.

---

# The spine has already carried us away from the opening room. This node was a
# root until ADR-302 D17: while the walk restored a save, its hooks displaced
# the harness's own restart hook and the reboot never fired for any node with a
# parent (issue #227). Re-execution has no hooks to displace.
> look
[OK: contains "Fountain Court"]

# Restart: the ack renders (never "I don't understand that."), then the
# harness reboots onto a fresh ChordStory
> restart
[OK: contains "The story restarts."]
[OK: not contains "I don't understand"]
[OK: not contains "Restart failed"]

# Fresh boot: back at the opening location, world fully rebuilt
> look
[OK: contains "Iron Gates"]

# The rebuilt world plays normally
> north
[OK: contains "Gravel Drive"]
